{"title":"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(A_bit_of_light_bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (A bit of light bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Uses_Analytical_Monotone)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Uses Analytical Monotone)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For what values of the variable <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> does the following inequality hold:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/8/cf8aa03d2cfb5932885cc52f52c98f7e1bd5df0b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{4x^2}{(1 - \\sqrt {2x + 1})^2} &lt; 2x + 9 \\ ?\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"44\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/4/be4cff4344f51344cde270d25925e8460d7f6052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -\\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{a^2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"103\" height=\"39\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f7cf108e9ba8a198529b7de54e3f432a34c70a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ge0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"16\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/f/5ef2d9a4de6f8b44fb42b51a85496506115953ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{a^2}{2}\\right)^2}{\\left(1-\\sqrt{1+2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{a^2}{2}\\right)}\\right)^2}&lt;2\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{a^2}{2}\\right)+9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -35px\" width=\"370\" height=\"78\" />\n</p><p>After simplifying, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/679cb2f2f5e16466928e5a8b0a85d8ea784d8302.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+1)^2&lt;a^2+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>So\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cd5315f889b438e1d88373356bb79b449d24246.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+2a+1&lt;a^2+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"161\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/a/9fae87a2b21ff9926dd074270dcd07e30acf5e3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a&lt;\\frac{7}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"45\" height=\"37\" /> and hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d52ae8ef784dda25cbeb242faa887188a2b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{2} \\le x&lt;\\frac{45}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"106\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> makes the LHS indeterminate.\n</p><p>So, answer: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77d52ae8ef784dda25cbeb242faa887188a2b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{2} \\le x&lt;\\frac{45}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"106\" height=\"37\" />, except <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/9/d79c96e270e148516fb5dd4a73725d8be87c80c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\neq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />, then the LHS is defined and rewrites as follows:\n</p><p>\\begin{align*} \n\\frac{4x^2}{(1 - \\sqrt{2x + 1})^2} &amp;= \\biggl(\\frac{2x}{1 - \\sqrt{2x + 1}}\\biggl)^2 \\\\\n&amp;= \\biggl( \\frac{2x}{1 - \\sqrt{2x + 1}} \\cdot \\frac{1 + \\sqrt{2x + 1}}{1 + \\sqrt{2x + 1}} \\biggl)^2 \\\\\n&amp;= (1 + \\sqrt{2x + 1})^2 \\\\\n&amp;= 2x + 2\\sqrt{2x + 1} + 2.\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>The inequality therefore holds if and only if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/08796af603cb8aa93b675a6a04d68a12d8291481.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x + 2\\sqrt{2x + 1} + 2 &lt; 2x + 9.\\]\" width=\"226\" height=\"18\" />\nor\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb165584c307b4d3427d010f7d62a123d9b7d97.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt{2x + 1} &lt; \\frac{7}{2}.\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/7/e970ba0902681746a64df5cf75f280f29ff16140.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x + 1 &lt; 49/4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"113\" height=\"20\" /> and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73db2d87b7b3bea70ed5097f3b17848f1796012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; 45/8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" />. But if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d9349aa4c8168d48252a4f0ea15bed7471bdd3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; -1/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> then the inequality makes no sense, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db5f21fd1eff2d427767eef451021dd2c4436e0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{2x + 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"21\" /> is imaginary. So the original inequality holds iff <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820dc1f799413e175ebb726683ece8352736459a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-1/2, 0) \\cup (0, 45/8).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28A_bit_of_light_bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(A_bit_of_light_bash)\">Solution 3 (A bit of light bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (A bit of light bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We consider when does the equality holds: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/1/73136cd3d6718c00d9216b8ae2a9016ad298d20a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4x^2}{(1 - \\sqrt {2x + 1})^2} = 2x + 9\\]\" width=\"195\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/6/a36516d173b3acb2bdeb522d0bb272ced04cb977.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[4x^2 = (2x+9)(1 - \\sqrt{2x+1})^2 \\Rightarrow 4x^2 = (2x+9)(2x+2-2\\sqrt{2x+1})\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Noting that we can cancel out the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/7/4675e27bb11d6efd975189436e433aaaf1677af2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />, we expand RHS and obtain: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22de314bcdca7ecbf74fdf3191cba843b19af3b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^2 = 4x^2 + 22x + 18 - (4x+18)\\sqrt{2x+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"333\" height=\"23\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/3/69383dfb8a266322ff6326bc59b850c8dc5f98ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4x+18)\\sqrt{2x+1} = 22x + 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"235\" height=\"23\" />, squaring both sides again, we yield:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/b/e0b7db7bd41a1a592b50392f2a56d8c5f40d81aa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[32x^3 + 304x^2 + 792x + 324 = 484x^2 + 792x + 324 \\Rightarrow 32x^3 = 180x^2 \\Rightarrow x^2(32x-180) = 0\\]\" width=\"647\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>From here we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/a/e3aa9b554da9ade707fb644f991edeb4eaf92bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\{0, \\frac{45}{8}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />, but when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/3/2d348bde3e15456e71734dc2c56fc7425c95927f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, the original expression is undefined as denominator is 0. Therefore, the only valid solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db590da9abcca821e65cf28148c94651768c53af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{45}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"59\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Then we consider the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/b/57b0413e6613d134ea30b2e4fde5c7994c914dd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\frac{4x^2}{(1 - \\sqrt {2x + 1})^2} - (2x + 9) = (1+\\sqrt{2x+1})^2-(2x+9)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"502\" height=\"47\" />, we aim to find the derivative of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />, which is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/a/a5a683ecd91ceedf906fbbeba40af130e395a7b5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f&#39;(x) = \\frac{2(1+\\sqrt{2x+1})}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}-2 = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}+2-2 = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2x+1}} &gt; 0\\]\" width=\"503\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Therefore we established that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bbad379658bd32e9b6479bbd666b93a96e6b48ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is monotonous and increasing. We are asked to find the values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80dd40e13b8ea55bf076c52db4ea542aa63cd96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4x^2}{(1 - \\sqrt{2x + 1})^2} &lt; 2x + 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"200\" height=\"47\" />, in other words, we are finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3f454ff06ec13f6d6c7c85957b07840049a0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />. By the monotonous and increasing property of the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3f454ff06ec13f6d6c7c85957b07840049a0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/d/d7d92302bbf506ccb12d5213b2caa43aec1ec3d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;\\frac{45}{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>However, there are two other special restrictions:\n</p><p>1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> cannot be 0, as that will result in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842650e9dc2e60349576e519428d19103f548710.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1 - \\sqrt{2x + 1})^2 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"23\" />, making the fraction indeterminate.\n</p><p>2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/1/2e123f2e8435226db3aea2e217dc9b599a1b3a80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac3ad73d2d28e7b3ca1b0a8cc91953b55dc74cb5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+1 \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> so that the square root is determinate.\n</p><p>In conclusion, inequality hold for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/9/67992caa34b936fa4de3a8ce41853a565dcfcc50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{x \\in [-\\frac{1}{2}, 0) \\cup (0, \\frac{45}{8})}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"176\" height=\"49\" />.\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:IDKHowtoaddsolution&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"User:IDKHowtoaddsolution (page does not exist)\">IDKHowtoaddsolution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Uses_Analytical_Monotone.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Uses_Analytical_Monotone)\">Solution 4 (Uses Analytical Monotone)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Uses Analytical Monotone)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since left-hand side needs to be well-defined, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/9/df92125891101cd0a285f7d9c615c36661fdb50a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />. Also, observe <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/d/55d152d0301f6d37abbd1d7e5efaca359c25ed01.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{4x^2}{(1-\\sqrt{1+2x})^2} = (1+\\sqrt{1+2x})^2.\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"45\" />Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d501e90bc8d7e4e94b2e3008d904d04d939ecb65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=(1+\\sqrt{1+2x})^2 - 2x-9=2\\sqrt{1+2x}-7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"384\" height=\"23\" />. Then, since that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2ba57c2738a318a9a95c1a2a53691ee1581875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"60\" height=\"37\" /> is a solution is verifiable, we consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d391cb8ab99f6cbd75a30a3efd28be55ba8bcece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;-\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Derivative\" title=\"Derivative\">derivative</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f75dab07a3ea634f7b704e3bbe67f310174a2da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"72\" height=\"43\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d391cb8ab99f6cbd75a30a3efd28be55ba8bcece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&gt;-\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"64\" height=\"38\" />, this expression evidently is non-negative, thus showing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> is strictly increasing. Two final observations are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/3/33371d05b0ddb900fb61d4c711f22d25f0d494a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(\\frac{45}{8})=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"82\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/f/fbff8c2d6247813a08aab2e4c24e40178d8e1bcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> is not defined. Thus, our range of solutions is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b51af69deb1af88498996c83195bd5291ca8ab9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left[-\\frac{1}{2}, 0\\right)\\cup\\left(0, -\\frac{1}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"159\" height=\"45\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO\" title=\"1960 IMO\">1960 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017053718\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal 